---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import PageHeader from '../components/PageHeader.astro';
import { site } from '../data/site';

const base = import.meta.env.BASE_URL.replace(/\/$/, '');
const lastUpdated = 'October 4, 2026';
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Privacy Policy | Benaya Tech"
  description="How Benaya Tech collects, uses, and protects the information you share when you visit our site or request smart-home, Wi-Fi, security, or installation service."
>
  <PageHeader
    title="Privacy Policy"
    sub={`How we handle the information you share with us. Last updated ${lastUpdated}.`}
  />

  <section class="bg-white py-16">
    <div class="container mx-auto px-4 max-w-3xl article-content">
      <p>
        This policy explains how {site.name} (“we,” “us,” or “our”) collects, uses, and shares
        information when you visit this website or contact us about work on your home or business.
        Questions about this policy may be directed to <a href={site.emailHref}>{site.email}</a>.
      </p>

      <h2>Information you give us</h2>
      <p>When you submit our request form, we collect what you enter:</p>
      <ul>
        <li>Your name, email address, and phone number</li>
        <li>Your city or service area</li>
        <li>Whether the project is for a home or a business</li>
        <li>Property or business type, number of locations, and your desired timeline</li>
        <li>The services you select and anything you write in the message field</li>
      </ul>
      <p>
        We also retain correspondence you send by phone, text, or email, together with the notes,
        configurations, and documentation produced while planning and completing your project.
      </p>

      <h2>Information collected automatically</h2>
      <p>
        We do not use cookies, analytics, advertising pixels, or any other tracking on this site.
        We do not build visitor profiles.
      </p>
      <p>
        Our hosting provider and the networks that deliver our fonts and one JavaScript library
        automatically record standard technical details — including IP address, browser type, and
        the pages requested — in order to deliver the site and protect it from abuse. This logging
        is performed by those providers and occurs on any site that uses such services.
      </p>

      <h2>Companies that process information for us</h2>
      <ul>
        <li><strong>Formspree</strong> — receives and delivers your request form submissions</li>
        <li><strong>GitHub Pages</strong> — hosts this website</li>
        <li><strong>Google Fonts</strong> — serves the typefaces used on this site</li>
        <li><strong>jsDelivr</strong> — serves a small JavaScript library used for menus and forms</li>
      </ul>
      <p>
        We do not sell or rent your personal information, and we do not share it for targeted
        advertising. We may share information when the law requires it, or when it is needed to
        establish or defend a legal claim.
      </p>

      <h2>How we use your information</h2>
      <ul>
        <li>To respond to your request, ask follow-up questions, and prepare an estimate</li>
        <li>To schedule, perform, document, and support the work</li>
        <li>To send messages about your specific project, appointment, or invoice</li>
        <li>To send marketing email, but only if you have asked us to</li>
        <li>To keep business records and meet tax, accounting, and legal obligations</li>
      </ul>

      <h2>Email and your consent</h2>
      <p>
        The marketing checkbox on our request form is optional and is never pre-selected. Leaving
        it unchecked has no effect on your request, your pricing, or the service you receive.
      </p>
      <p>
        If you do opt in, you can withdraw at any time using the unsubscribe link in any marketing
        email, or by emailing <a href={site.emailHref}>{site.email}</a>. Either way, we will still
        send the messages needed to handle your request and complete your project — such as
        scheduling confirmations, estimates, and invoices.
      </p>

      <h2>How long we retain information</h2>
      <p>
        We retain request and project records for as long as necessary for the purposes described
        above and to meet legal, tax, and accounting requirements. Information that is no longer
        needed is deleted or stripped of details that identify you.
      </p>

      <h2>Security</h2>
      <p>
        This site is served over an encrypted HTTPS connection, and access to request and project
        records is limited to personnel who require it to perform the work. No website or method of
        transmission is completely secure, and we cannot guarantee absolute security. Please do not
        send passwords or alarm codes by email; we will arrange a more secure method where needed.
      </p>

      <h2>Your choices</h2>
      <p>
        You may request access to the information we hold about you, ask us to correct it, or ask
        us to delete it. You may also opt out of marketing email at any time. Contact{' '}
        <a href={site.emailHref}>{site.email}</a> and we will respond within a reasonable period.
        We may first need to verify your identity, and we may retain information we are required to
        keep for legal or accounting purposes.
      </p>

      <h2>Children</h2>
      <p>
        This site is intended for adults arranging work on a property. It is not directed to
        children under 13, and we do not knowingly collect their information. If you believe a
        child has provided us with information, contact us and we will delete it.
      </p>

      <h2>Changes to this policy</h2>
      <p>
        If we change this policy, we will post the new version here and update the date at the top
        of the page.
      </p>

      <h2>Contact us</h2>
      <p>
        {site.name}<br />
        Email: <a href={site.emailHref}>{site.email}</a><br />
        Phone: <a href={site.phoneHref}>{site.phoneDisplay}</a><br />
        Serving Northern Virginia
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>
